@startuml
!include style.puml
skinparam ArrowFontStyle plain

participant ":LogicManager" as Logic LOGIC_COLOR
participant ":BackupCommand" as Backup LOGIC_COLOR
participant "model:Model" as Model MODEL_COLOR
participant ":JsonAddressBookStorage" as Storage STORAGE_COLOR
participant "<<class>>\nAtomicFileWriter" as Writer STORAGE_COLOR

note over Logic, Backup
AddressBookParser accepts backup without arguments.
HistoryAction.NONE: no checkpoint, history commit or employee-file save.
end note
Logic -> Backup : execute(model)
activate Backup
Backup -> Model : getAddressBook()
Model --> Backup : complete roster
Backup -> Backup : timestamp from local clock\nchoose counter 0000000000
loop retry while destination is occupied
    Backup -> Backup : createStorage(backupPath)
    Backup -> Storage : saveNewAddressBook(roster)
    activate Storage
    Storage -> Storage : serialise complete JSON
    Storage -> Writer : writeNew(path, bytes)
    activate Writer
    note right of Writer
Create parents and protected sibling temporary file.
Write and force bytes, then publish with a new hard link.
Never replace an existing destination.
end note
    alt snapshot published
        Writer --> Storage : return
        Storage --> Backup : return
        note right of Backup : Leave retry loop.
    else FileAlreadyExistsException
        Writer --> Storage : collision
        Storage --> Backup : collision
        Backup -> Backup : verify occupied path with NOFOLLOW_LINKS\nincrement counter
    end
    deactivate Writer
    deactivate Storage
end
Backup --> Logic : CommandResult("Backed up <count> employee(s) to <path>")
deactivate Backup
note over Backup, Writer
Other I/O failures produce the backup-specific CommandException.
Earlier snapshots, employee data, view and history remain unchanged.
end note
@enduml
